# New (RESULTS.md, finding 1): the power goes 40 ms after the first addition acknowledged from
# step 20 on, while the swap task 164 is between its two commits: the swapped index mapping is
# committed, its succeeded status is not. The restart runs the swap again, so sa and sb end as
# after an even number of swaps while the queue counts 21 succeeded swaps. The same schedule
# also empties two acknowledged additions' payloads (finding 2), which the verdict line names;
# the swap's lines are in hydo report --details <run dir>. A SIGKILL does the same in Docker
# (native/swap-twice.sh). The moment moves with the image's bytes: on the image before the
# build parameter dumps, the cut 2 ms after the event gave this finding.
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bugs are fixed)
disk=none | run A=meili.add_acked@20+40:cut
